(4424306, 636075, 811, '<td valign="top">I like how the road leads up and into the frame.  Also, the trees do give a nice "frame" for the shot.  However, there are some things that could make this a much stronger photo, I think.  Move more to the center of the road (if there is little or not traffic, obviously).  I think that will make it feel more balanced and not so chopped off on the left.  Also, it seems to have a bluish cast to me.  Maybe "warm up" the white balance just a hair.  Finally, take advantage of the size.  Your shot is about 1/2 or a 1/3 what it could be.  Ask in the forums, or look at the tutorials if you don''t know how to resize for dpc.</td>', 'I like how the road leads up and into the frame.  Also, the trees do give a nice "frame" for the shot.  However, there are some things that could make this a much stronger photo, I think.  Move more to the center of the road (if there is little or not traffic, obviously).  I think that will make it feel more balanced and not so chopped off on the left.  Also, it seems to have a bluish cast to me.  Maybe "warm up" the white balance just a hair.  Finally, take advantage of the size.  Your shot is about 1/2 or a 1/3 what it could be.  Ask in the forums, or look at the tutorials if you don''t know how to resize for dpc.', '2008-01-25 12:33:14.000000', NULL, 1),
