(4442551, 634194, 67855, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe:</b></div><hr/><i> oversaturation is "in" eh?  to me it actually detracts from an otherwise terrific image.<br/>j </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi<br/> <br/>I agree with you about the oversaturation, which makes lose some materials(subject). For my personal custom(usage) I shall not have post processing as it. But the entry is for a challenge and seduce most large people.<br/>I adjusted the saturation, levels etc.<br/> <br/>Basic editing : You may :<br/>* saturate, desaturate or change the colors of your entry, but no selections are allowed.<br/> <br/>Thanks :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-31 10:42:28.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe: oversaturation is "in" eh?  to me it actually detracts from an otherwise terrific image.j  Hi I agree with you about the oversaturation, which makes lose some materials(subject). For my personal custom(usage) I shall not have post processing as it. But the entry is for a challenge and seduce most large people.I adjusted the saturation, levels etc. Basic editing : You may :* saturate, desaturate or change the colors of your entry, but no selections are allowed. Thanks :)', '2008-01-31 06:15:44.000000', '2008-01-31 10:42:28.000000', 0),
(4442626, 635175, 63269, '<td valign="top">Fabulous! I love those green eyes, the way they match with the frame... and congradulations on getting the cat to cooporate. ;)</td>', 'Fabulous! I love those green eyes, the way they match with the frame... and congradulations on getting the cat to cooporate. ;)', '2008-01-31 07:10:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4442643, 635909, 63269, '<td valign="top">I really like what you''ve got here... my only suggestion would be to get rid of the color and go to black and white. I personally think the colors aren''t doing much to help the photo - they''re all very bright, random colors, and they''re only around the edges of things. But then again maybe you wanted that effect, with the little bits and hints of color here and there...yes, now that I look at it again, I can see where someone might like it. It''s almost like a hint of a rainbow is spillng into the tunnel after the person. I still would have fully desaturated it though. ;)Overall it''s definitely a great shot, with splendid composition and ligting! :)</td>', 'I really like what you''ve got here... my only suggestion would be to get rid of the color and go to black and white. I personally think the colors aren''t doing much to help the photo - they''re all very bright, random colors, and they''re only around the edges of things. But then again maybe you wanted that effect, with the little bits and hints of color here and there...yes, now that I look at it again, I can see where someone might like it. It''s almost like a hint of a rainbow is spillng into the tunnel after the person. I still would have fully desaturated it though. ;)Overall it''s definitely a great shot, with splendid composition and ligting! :)', '2008-01-31 07:17:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4442666, 635326, 63269, '<td valign="top">I love this. The elegant, subtle mood you have captured here is glorious. I really like the composition... Well done. When I read the title "Trees of <i>Snowfall</i>," I almost subconsciously started looking for the snow, saw it, and really liked it. Even if I hadn''t seen the title though I think I still would have realized it was snow. And since I''ve always wanted to get a picture of a winter scene and somehow capture the falling snow as well, I would have been thrilled anyway. <br/> <br/>Just a thought. <br/>Great photo! :)</td>', 'I love this. The elegant, subtle mood you have captured here is glorious. I really like the composition... Well done. When I read the title "Trees of Snowfall," I almost subconsciously started looking for the snow, saw it, and really liked it. Even if I hadn''t seen the title though I think I still would have realized it was snow. And since I''ve always wanted to get a picture of a winter scene and somehow capture the falling snow as well, I would have been thrilled anyway.  Just a thought. Great photo! :)', '2008-01-31 07:24:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4442677, 636763, 63269, '<td valign="top">Fantastic! I love the shallow dof here, and it works so well. I personally might have added just a touch of contrast... but I also love the richness of the green, and your use of framing is quite clever. It should have scored higher! :)</td>', 'Fantastic! I love the shallow dof here, and it works so well. I personally might have added just a touch of contrast... but I also love the richness of the green, and your use of framing is quite clever. It should have scored higher! :)', '2008-01-31 07:27:46.000000', NULL, 0),
