(4449188, 635867, 76103, '<td valign="top">omg I think I''ve been there. We went to this whole Arch National Park when I was in Moab with my dad''s best friend and hiked up this slab of rock in the beating sun... so cool to see the place again!</td>', 'omg I think I''ve been there. We went to this whole Arch National Park when I was in Moab with my dad''s best friend and hiked up this slab of rock in the beating sun... so cool to see the place again!', '2008-02-01 23:14:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4449794, 636544, 68035, '<td valign="top">Shannon<br/> <br/>Great to see you entering another challenge and congratulations on the impressive top 30 finish.  This was one of my favourite shots in the challenge, as not only did it perfectly fit the challenge description but it did so in a wonderfully unique way.  I love the symettry of the image and the wonderful range of tones in the black and white conversion (somehow you have got very black blacks and very white whites, but the shot does not appear harsh and has a gorgeous softness to it that compliments the image completely)<br/> <br/>Fantastic photo</td>', 'Shannon Great to see you entering another challenge and congratulations on the impressive top 30 finish.  This was one of my favourite shots in the challenge, as not only did it perfectly fit the challenge description but it did so in a wonderfully unique way.  I love the symettry of the image and the wonderful range of tones in the black and white conversion (somehow you have got very black blacks and very white whites, but the shot does not appear harsh and has a gorgeous softness to it that compliments the image completely) Fantastic photo', '2008-02-02 06:58:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4449797, 637070, 68035, '<td valign="top">Well I see from the OOBIE and Posthumous threads that this was a photo that really touched some people, and for me even if a lot of people did not get it this is so much better than having everyone go "hmmmmmm its OK".  <br/> <br/>Very clever take on the challenge, and I love the sharpness of the emerging sticks.  Really top class B&amp;W conversion as well.  Overall an image that will have a lot more long term appeal than many that finished above it in the challenge<br/> <br/></td>', 'Well I see from the OOBIE and Posthumous threads that this was a photo that really touched some people, and for me even if a lot of people did not get it this is so much better than having everyone go "hmmmmmm its OK".   Very clever take on the challenge, and I love the sharpness of the emerging sticks.  Really top class B&W conversion as well.  Overall an image that will have a lot more long term appeal than many that finished above it in the challenge ', '2008-02-02 07:02:14.000000', NULL, 0),
